# TLS passthrough routing table.
#
# Install as /etc/haproxy/passthrough.conf. This file is NOT tracked in the
# repository — it names your own hostnames and internal ports, which are yours,
# not this project's.
#
# One line per domain:
#
#   <sni-hostname>    <backend-target>
#
# Connections whose TLS SNI matches the hostname are handed to the target with
# the handshake untouched, so that service keeps terminating its own TLS. The
# hub's own domains are unaffected; anything matching neither is silent-dropped.
#
# After editing, apply with:
#
#   sudo /opt/notification-hub/bin/passthrough.sh sync
#
# which regenerates HAProxy's map and backend files, validates the result, and
# reloads with no dropped connections.

# domain                     target
#servenet.example.com        127.0.0.1:441
#mooz.example.com            127.0.0.1:440
